KNOWNBUG: [dcl.init.aggr]/2,5 -- per-element brace-initialization of a class
array with a user-provided constructor (`S a[N]{ {a}, {b} }`) currently aborts:
the brace elements are wrapped into an array expression whose operands are never
type-checked, and indexing that array during construction yields a nil-typed
expression that crashes simplification.  Affects known- and unknown-bound
arrays alike.  Flip to CORE once each element is constructed directly from its
initializer-clause.
